From: j7 battery
Subject: a5xelte: an S2MU004 fuel gauge driver, and SweetBattery on A5XELTE

The battery icon fell back to powerd's 1 % because nothing published a power source: SweetBattery
was compiled for SWEET and HEROLTE only, and this board has no gauge driver.  The J7 Prime's
gauge is the S2MU004 block at 0x3B on i2c@13830000 (Samsung sec-fuelgauge, sibling of the S2MPU03
PMIC that a5xelte_touch.c already talks to).  bsd/dev/a5xelte_battery.c reads RSOC 0x08,
RVBAT 0x04, RCUR_CC 0x06 and RBATCAP 0x0e over a polled S3C2440-layout transfer, the same
sequence the touch bus uses on this phone, and SweetBattery publishes it (3300 mAh design
capacity) through the existing IOPMPowerSource path.  j7fg=0 disables the probe.

